{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-479561-r4630576","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Seblak","sourcePageId":479561,"sourceRevision":"4630576","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-14T09:10:43Z","sourceRevisionUser":"A Sulaiman Z","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Seblak&oldid=4630576","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T14:16:00.540Z","sourceCategories":[],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"521d3bcef385910e2ba00c838fb99c49e29a792e43059a8a39941c20f0a5c58e","sourceWikitext":"{{Incomplete recipe|reason=missing links, missing categories, needs formatting}}__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Indonesian recipes\n| Servings = 5\n| Image = [[File:Seblak di Garut.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Seblak''' is a traditional snack from Sunda. This food is commonly found in West Java Province, especially in Bandung, Garut, and Tasikmalaya. It is made mainly from crackers with ''kencur'' (aromatic ginger) and chili as the main spices. Seblak is well-known for its spicy taste and easy preparation. \n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 250 grams of raw [[Cookbook: Cracker|crackers]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|chicken eggs]]\n* 1/4 kg of boiled [[Cookbook: Chicken|chicken meat]] (cut into small pieces)\n* 2 packs of [[Cookbook: Instant Noodles|instant noodles]]\n* 2 pieces of kencur ([[Cookbook: Ginger|aromatic ginger]])\n* 2 [[Cookbook: Shallot|shallots]] \n* 2 [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]] of [[Cookbook: Garlic|garlic]]\n* 100 grams of fresh [[Cookbook: Chili|chili]]\n* 1 tablespoon of [[Cookbook: Broth and Stock|chicken broth]] powder\n* 1 [[Cookbook: Teaspoon|teaspoon]] of [[Cookbook: Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1/2 teaspoon of [[Cookbook: Salt|salt]]\n* 2 tablespoons of [[Cookbook: Vegetable Oil|cooking oil]] (for sautéing)\n* 200 ml of [[Cookbook: Water|water]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Prepare all the ingredients.  \n# Blend ''kencur'' (aromatic ginger), shallots, and garlic. Add a little salt.  \n# Blend the chili separately.\n# Heat the oil in a pan. \n# Sauté the blended kencur, shallots, and garlic until fragrant and cooked.\n# Add the blended chili, then stir until it smells fragrant.\n# Next, pour in the water.\n# Add salt, chicken broth powder, and sugar to taste.\n# Put in the crackers and boiled chicken pieces, then stir until cooked.\n# Add the instant noodles, and stir again until everything is well-cooked.\n# Pour it into a bowl according to your preferred portion. \n# Seblak is ready to serve.\n\n== Recommendation ==\n\n* You can add various toppings to your seblak, such as meatballs, sausages, vegetables, or other seafood ingredients as you like.\n* You can also make seblak with soup or dry-style. If you want to make seblak with soup, make sure to add enough water so it doesn’t dry out.\n\n== See also ==\n{{Wikipedia|Seblak}}\n\n[[Category:Sundanese recipes]]\n[[Category:Indonesian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using crackers]]\n[[Category:Chili recipes]]\n[[Category:Aromatic ginger recipes]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Seblak","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"5","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"250 grams of raw crackers","sourceText":"250 grams of raw crackers","amountText":"250 grams of raw crackers","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","na